  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an array `nums` of **distinct** positive integers, output *the number of tuples* `(a, b, c, d)` *such that* `a * b = c * d` *where* `a`*,* `b`*,* `c`*, and* `d` *are elements of* `nums`*, and* `a != b != c != d`*.*\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [2,3,4,6]\nOutput: 8\nExplanation: There are 8 valid tuples:\n(2,6,3,4) , (2,6,4,3) , (6,2,3,4) , (6,2,4,3)\n(3,4,2,6) , (4,3,2,6) , (3,4,6,2) , (4,3,6,2)\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,4,5,10]\nOutput: 16\nExplanation: There are 16 valid tuples:\n(1,10,2,5) , (1,10,5,2) , (10,1,2,5) , (10,1,5,2)\n(2,5,1,10) , (2,5,10,1) , (5,2,1,10) , (5,2,10,1)\n(2,10,4,5) , (2,10,5,4) , (10,2,4,5) , (10,2,5,4)\n(4,5,2,10) , (4,5,10,2) , (5,4,2,10) , (5,4,10,2)\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 104`\n* All elements in `nums` are **distinct**.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
